    "Provenance record for every Claude Code configuration file vendored into this repo from outside.",
    "Hand-maintained: the skill that used to write this file (setup-matt-pocock-skills) was removed as unused in claude-config-earns-its-place. That is only acceptable because scripts/check-plugin-sync.mjs verifies it \u2014 a hand-maintained lock with nothing checking it reads as a guarantee it cannot give.",
    "upstreamHash: sha256 of the UPSTREAM source file as it was at install time. It is provenance, not integrity: it does NOT hash the installed copy and cannot be verified locally without refetching. Version 1 of this file called it computedHash, which implied the opposite \u2014 every recorded value mismatched the installed file it appeared to describe, and nothing noticed because nothing checked.",
    "installedHash: sha256 of the file actually present in this repo. This is what the check verifies, and what detects a local edit to a vendored file.",
    "supportingFiles: listed for completeness but deliberately NOT hashed. Only SKILL.md is covered. Stated as a limitation rather than left implied.",
    "agents.*.locallyEdited: true means the frontmatter was deliberately rewritten for this repo (tools, model, slug name, trigger description). Divergence from upstream is EXPECTED there \u2014 do not 'restore' these from the pack."
